WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:03.239
Now more than ever we are exposed to a plethora of ideas,

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.529
methods, and suggestions about life

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:12.508
The Internet has made it so we can consume and/or share a seemingly unending amount of content on the topic of living most effectively.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.719
However,

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:18.358
simultaneously, this access to information has also allowed the consumer to realize just how

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.529
conflicting most ideas are. In the West, over the last several decades or so,

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:25.859
not only has the popularity of traditional religion reduced as a result,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.580
but for many, the

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:35.279
increasing access to information has revealed that the world is basically without any discernible truth, and most ideas about how to live are inconclusive

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:42.329
and unreliable. It is fair to speculate that this could perhaps be a major contributing factor to the modern world's increasing levels of anxiety,

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:44.520
cynicism, and disillusion.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:50.309
It's as if we live in a constant debate over what is true and good, and every time we're about to come to a decision,

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:54.029
someone says something new or different and starts the whole debate over.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:01:01.320
Dealing with and choosing between conflicting ideas of how to live has always been an issue for the individual. But in the modern world, where

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.400
conflicting ideas are constantly smacking us in the face, now more than ever

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.880
we can often find ourselves

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:14.070
failing in our attempt to find footing in this reality. For every time a new idea renders our previously withheld ideas wrong or inferior,

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.919
we lose a little hope in trusting any ideas at all.

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:20.339
No religion, philosophy, science, government,

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:28.258
parent/teacher, or self-help advice can seemingly piece together any truth or answer to life that will rid us of our uncertainty or hardship.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:33.810
Perhaps then it is not a truth or answer that we must seek to remove life's uncertainty and hardship.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.259
Rather, It is a template of wisdom that we must experience life's

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.059
uncertainty and hardship through. In an attempt to find this we will look to the movement of

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:49.889
Existentialism, a movement that started in the West during the 19th century at the onset of a decreasing popularity in traditional religions.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.869
Specifically, we will look to one of the most renowned existential thinkers: Jean-Paul Sartre.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:02:00.360
Jean-Paul Sartre was born in 1905 in Paris, France and is considered to be one of the main

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:08.460
popularizers of existential thinking. He wrote numerous books that define much of what existentialism is based on, most popularly "Being and

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.040
Nothingness" which describes the crux of existential thought. For Sartre and the

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:20.329
Existentialists, life has no fundamental meaning or truth beyond what is created by our decisions and actions within it. The core of

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:26.839
Existential thought can be summarized with the notion that as humans, our existence precedes our essence. In other words,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:29.780
we have no predetermined purpose, and consequently,

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.680
there is no specific way to live.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:38.450
Rather, both purpose and a way to live comes only from living life and making choices within it. And for Sartre and the Existentialists,

00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:41.389
we are free to choose what we do. In a way,

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:46.190
it's as if we are all given a slab of clay at birth and it is up to us to decide what we mold it

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:46.860
into.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:53.809
However, Sartre points out that as we grow older, we become more and more influenced by those around us, and we second-guess what we have

00:02:53.810 --> 00:03:00.199
started molding and begin to copy what others have already made an attempt to ensure that we are making something good or right.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.399
However, for Sartre there is no right or wrong way to mold the clay. Rather

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.060
there are endless ways, all

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:12.110
equally absurd, all equally meaningless, and all equally worthy of molding to the individual molding it.

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:17.449
This freedom to mold life any way we wish, coupled with a deep desire for wanting to mold it as best we possibly

00:03:17.609 --> 00:03:21.169
can, is what brings on such high levels of anxiety in life.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.580
"Man is condemned to be free; because once thrown into the world, he is responsible for everything

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.879
he does." Sartre writes. In other words,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.399
we lack any ability to know if our choices are good or bad or right or wrong because for whatever reason,

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.709
our human condition does not permit us to.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:40.789
We can never really know if what we choose to make of our life is what's best for us,

00:03:40.889 --> 00:03:45.319
nor can anyone else know, yet we still must live our life and make decisions within it.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:51.829
This premise is revealed very clearly under the spotlight of the internet, for the widespread access to information reveals

00:03:51.829 --> 00:03:53.549
very little beyond contradiction.

00:03:53.549 --> 00:04:01.189
We are now in an age where we find ourselves with seemingly endless information and potential solutions to dealing with life, yet increasing anxieties,

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:03.299
depressions, and confusions.

00:04:03.299 --> 00:04:10.189
Existentialism would suggest that this is because there are no timeless, definitive answers to human life that apply to everyone. We can't make any choice

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.919
knowing for sure if it will or won't be what's best for us,

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:16.879
and so we should not look for or expect any ultimate answers that will.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:24.070
This doesn't mean that we should not engage in, consume, consider, or share ideas, research, and philosophies about life,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:27.879
but it is to say that we should be skeptical in our considerations, and mitigate our

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:35.109
expectations accordingly. In many ways, ideas for how to live are just as much art and entertainment as they are prescriptions for how to live.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:41.709
No matter how wise a piece of advice may seem, there is nothing to suggest that anyone else can form a better idea for how

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:46.750
to live than one's own self. So what do we do if there's no accessible truth, or ultimate way to live?

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:50.410
How do we live if no one can tell us or provide us with a clear way?

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:57.819
Existentialism suggests one primary template of wisdom to deal with this uncertainty of life that we are left with. For the Existentialist,

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.249
there is a constantly changing state of existence that we

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.940
must flow with, accepting the absurdity and meaninglessness of it all and

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.140
transmuting the chaos of life into our own unique experience and personal meaning.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:16.570
"Man," Sartre writes "Can will nothing unless he has first understood that he must count on no one but himself; that he is alone, abandoned

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.560
on earth in the midst of his infinite

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.030
responsibilities, without help, with no other aim than the one he sets himself,

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.809
with no other destiny than the one he forges for himself on this earth."

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.319
It is the truth that we deem for ourselves and carry out

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:35.440
experimentally through our actions that defines what's true for us, for the truth of how to live is relative. In

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:39.999
the modern information age, a great many of us feel further and further disconnected.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:44.140
We seek a truth that will bring us in and resolve our confusion and alienation.

00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:49.419
When we don't find it, many of us begin to feel as though something is wrong and that we don't belong, and

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:53.709
perhaps that's because we don't, because no one does. Early on in life

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:58.600
we are given the idea that there is really only a couple ways to live. On these predetermined paths

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:04.570
we are told that there is an ultimate goal of perfection, truth, and happiness that we are striving towards. However,

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:09.580
perhaps it is more likely that there are endless ways of living, ways that we each have to determine for ourselves,

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:16.509
based on ourselves, and that none of what we do will equate to any sort of ultimate shared truth or meaning but rather a sense

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:24.039
of personal meaning and self fulfillment. When one realizes and accepts that there are no fundamental rules or truths in the world of human existence,

00:06:24.169 --> 00:06:30.159
the individual becomes self-aware of their freedom and realizes that they don't to do anything specific in life.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:34.659
We realize that we don't have to follow or agree with any of what we've been given. We can choose

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:39.189
otherwise. We don't have to meet the standards of anyone else's ideas for how to live, be it

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:46.119
our parents, friends, teachers, religions, or cultures. The pressure and anxiousness of constantly searching for the right way to live can be

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.590
alleviated, and instead

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:53.350
we can look inwards, consider how we wish to experience life, and work to mold ourselves and choices accordingly.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:59.559
We can use our uniquely assembled self to fulfill a uniquely assembled life, realizing our full potential,

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:04.149
accepting the uncertainties, and making the endurance of existence personally worth it.

